target/

# Written by the CI coverage step (`--out Xml` plus the tee it greps).
# Never committed: the number lives in the run summary and on Codecov, and a 200 KB
# report of one machine's run is not a fact about this repository.
cobertura.xml
coverage.log

# `CLAUDE.md` carries this repository's conventions, so it is tracked like any other
# document — and being tracked is what puts it under `scripts/check-docs.sh`, which
# reads `git ls-files` and could not see it before. That is not a detail: an untracked
# CLAUDE.md is a document with no executor, which is the condition every stale line
# this repository has found grew in.
#
# The negation is needed because a global ignore file excludes `CLAUDE.md` everywhere.
# A `.gitignore` inside the repository outranks `core.excludesFile`, so it bites.
# Verified rather than assumed: `git status --porcelain --ignored CLAUDE.md` reports
# `??` and not `!!`. (`git check-ignore -v` is the wrong test — it exits 0 when *any*
# pattern matches, a negation included, and only the leading `!` in its output says
# which kind matched.)
!CLAUDE.md

# The half of it that is about personal preferences rather than about Skylode — how he wants things
# explained, in which language. Useful to an assistant, meaningless to a contributor,
# and not this project's business. `CLAUDE.local.md` is the documented name for it,
# and no global rule covers that one.
CLAUDE.local.md
